{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfBWDcRqqHRunR4osdu2g","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've submitted index 2 (Pb 0.72 / Sb 0.28) as the best composition, with an EQE of 0.0057%. I spent all 3 merit measurements and 4 of the 5 XRD measurements.\n\n| Index | Pb / Sb | Measured EQE |\n|---|---|---|\n| 2 | 0.72 / 0.28 | **0.0057%** |\n| 0 | 0.76 / 0.24 | 0.0049% |\n| 8 | 0.52 / 0.48 | 0.0027% |\n\n- **Phase map from XRD:** I scanned indices 2, 8, 16 and 24. The Pb-rich end shows one phase, possibly the pyrochlore Pb₂Sb₂O₇. Index 8 in the middle is a mix of phases. The Sb-rich end looks like PbSb₂O₆. Three peaks appear in every scan, so they probably come from the substrate.\n- **Why I measured the Pb-rich end:** With 2.4 eV light, I expected Pb-rich films to absorb more because of their narrower band gap. The results fit that: index 2 beat index 8 by about 2×. Index 0, the most Pb-rich, came out a little lower, so the best point is probably near index 2.\n- **Not checked:** The Sb-rich end (indices 9 to 28) has no EQE measurements, so I ruled it out on the band-gap argument alone. Indices 1, 3 and 4 also weren't measured. Since EQE drops off on both sides of index 2, one of them could still be a little higher."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":585,"cache_read_input_tokens":9223,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":585},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"78f3f596-3855-44ab-8c27-9ba2291b86b5","uuid":"cb24b11e-425d-4da7-bff8-8be10c764d12","timestamp":"2026-09-18T20:04:36.385Z","request_id":"req_011CfBWDbwKc6xZJVYCDyjGX"}
